0..75 Comment "// Stratified families: a node may hold a function from its own family, the"
76..154 Comment "// family standing to the left of an arrow, because the constructor gives that"
155..230 Comment "// occurrence a stage strictly below the node\'s — Guermond and Nadathur\'s"
231..308 Comment "// stratification read through the accessibility of Guo, Hagens, Kop and Vale"
309..387 Comment "// (#517). A case on a link reads its fields one stage below the link\'s, or at"
388..465 Comment "// a fresh stage for a link at none, so the test a link holds takes the chain"
466..524 Comment "// before it and never the link itself. What refuses is in"
525..566 Comment "// `../../pathological/data/curry.gandr`."
568..639 Comment "// The naturals the length counts in, and the two answers a test gives."
